Z||000001||theogre||06-20-2000||10:09 PM||||very time consuming, not dificult. the info in the haynes book is fairly accurate on this. helps if you have 2 people. it's faily awkaward dropping the tank solo.<P>replace the fuel gauge sender while you're in there.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 06-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||dman||06-20-2000||10:25 PM||||Hi My7Fieros<P>How difficult? Depends on how mechanically inclined you are. Not too difficult in my opinion. Short description follows.<P>Jack up the rear real high (take usual safety precautions, good stands, chock front, etc). <P>Disconnect electrical connector to 3 wire harness that leads to the tank. It is a small 3 wire connector towards the middle of the firewall...careful since they tend to be brittle after all that heat over the years.<BR>Two of the wires are thick and are pinkish in colored, the third is a thinner gauge and is black. The black is the ground, the middle wire is the fuel level sender, the last wire is the positive lead going to the pump.<P>Drain tank. Many ways to do this. What I do is just disconnect the fuel line going to the filter and using some spare hose route it to to a gas container. Then I jump (hotwire) the fuel pump to empty the gas into the container.<P>Get underneath the car and you'll see that all of the hoses you will need to disconnect are at the rear end of the tank. Loosen the clamps, and disconnect the hoses. <P>Two straps hold the tank into place, each strap is secured with (I think) a 13millimeter nut. Undo the front strap first, then the rear strap.<P>You'll probably want to tilt the front of the tank so it rests on the ground, then carefully lower the rear and slide the tank out. If you lower the rear first you may cause some residual gas to leak out since the lines are located towards the rear.<P>Carefully remove the pump, sender, screen etc. Replace.<P>Installation is reverse.<P>Get yourself a Haynes or Chilton manual if you don't already have one. I would guess their description of the process is a little easier to follow than mine, they also have pictures.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||06-20-2000||10:29 PM||||super cool, thanx Dman...yes my roommate and I are mechanically inclined. Our Fieros NEVER go to the mechanic...all the work is done on them ourselves. This is one of the few things we have yet to do. Dosnt sound like too much of a problem. What Im not looking forward to is replacing the forward exhuast manifold on one of the 87 Gts...eek! But thats another post to come later..thanx again.||||reg||1
